<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Azerbaijan</h1><p class="st-meta">1991 CE – present · capital Baku</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The independent Republic of Azerbaijan on the Caspian Sea, an oil and gas producer whose post-Soviet history has been dominated by the Karabakh conflict.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan-ssr">Azerbaijan SSR</a> declared independence on 30 August 1991, confirmed by a constitutional act on 18 October 1991, and became fully sovereign with the dissolution of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> in December. It claimed descent from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan-democratic-republic">Azerbaijan Democratic Republic</a> of 1918-1920, whose flag it readopted, while war with Armenian forces over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagorno-karabakh">Nagorno-Karabakh</a> was already under way.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>After defeat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-nagorno-karabakh-war">First Karabakh War</a> and a 1994 ceasefire that left Armenian forces holding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karabakh">Karabakh</a> and surrounding districts, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heydar-aliyev">Heydar Aliyev</a>, president from 1993, built a strong presidential system, passed to his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilham-aliyev">Ilham Aliyev</a> in 2003. The 1994 Contract of the Century and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baku-tbilisi-ceyhan-pipeline">Baku-Tbilisi-Ceyhan</a> pipeline, opened in 2005, brought oil wealth and Western investment. The state is secular, with a Shia majority.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>In the 2020 war Azerbaijan regained much of the lost territory, and a 2023 offensive brought all of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karabakh">Karabakh</a> under its control, prompting the flight of its Armenian population. Peace talks with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/armenia">Armenia</a> continue.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/azerbaijan.jpg" alt="Azerbaijan" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: SKopp and others · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Azerbaijan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1991 CE – present</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Baku</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abulfaz Elchibey, Heydar Aliyev, Ilham Aliyev</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Shia Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Azerbaijani</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Azerbaijan</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Azerbaijan</dd></dl></aside></div>
